A||||32||Wes Janson||Is this unheard of or what?||||12||
Z||000000||Wes Janson||07-06-2000||06:22 PM||||Check this out. How about installing Delorean style hydraulic swing-up doors on my '84 Fiero?<P>Or is this a little too much? Let me hear some feedback on this one.<P>- Janson||||reg||12
Z||000001||StuGood||07-06-2000||06:26 PM||||Why not? I saw Red Green install remote control gull-wing doors on a rusted-out Ford Grenada using only duct tape and his neighbor's garage door opener  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !||||reg||12
Z||000002||Wes Janson||07-06-2000||06:36 PM||||Great! I'm glad I'm not the only one who thinks this is a cool idea. My friends didn't take to kindly to the notion, but what do they know? ;-)<P>Anyway, all I need to plan out now is to trade off my instrumentation guages with LCD and digital panels. That shood zoom that thing into the new millennium! (Which isn't until 2001)...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spyder||07-06-2000||08:17 PM||||It will be hard to do Gull Wings. They would take the window to have a facing. <BR>You can probably do  a Lambo type doors though. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||07-06-2000||08:18 PM||||How would you do it? Don't you need a frame around the window to attach hinges? I'd love to hear the plan.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||07-06-2000||08:32 PM||||Actually you could use two rectangular bars to go from the roof to the door.  On tinted windows you shouldn’t notice the bars if painted black. It would take a lot of extra bracing on the roof. <BR>But Anything Can Be Done!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DoorGull.JPG">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DoorGull2.JPG"> <P>Does anyone think that I have way too much time on my hands?lol<p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 07-06-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||80's BOY||07-06-2000||09:45 PM||||i'd go with lambo doors. i did a set of gullwings on an s-10 back in '95. we got the piano spring from a wrecked delorean in Ft. Worth. after that, welding and body work was a cinch.....as long as you have a door frame, which in this case you do not.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||07-06-2000||09:49 PM||||I've been thinking about that mod for a couple years now.. I'd definitely replace the door, or at least modify it a LOT with a frame from another vehicle.. I'm sure there's some other car that has a door frame that could be modified to fit the fiero door frame.. then you'd need to cut up the roof, and add t-tops.. but instead of removable panels, there would need to be custom fabricated panels attached to the top of the doors.. I think it would be a lot of work (not as much as lambo-style wing doors though) and cost quite a bit.. but I think it definitely could be done.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wes Janson||07-06-2000||10:35 PM||||So you're saying that it's possible to do a T-Top style with the Gull Wings?||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||07-07-2000||02:26 AM||||I don't see why it wouldn't be possible, with a bit of work.. there *might* be leaking problems around the upper door seals, and some of the wiring would need to be re-routed, as well as a new locking mechanism, new hinges, and a latch at the bottom of the door.. I think the new/modified door would be the hardest part.. the hinge would be fairly simple, and it would just need gas struts on either side of the hinge..<P>It would be a lot of work to do.. but it'd be worth it, if it was done correctly! in fact.. I wouldn't mind trying this sometime.. it'd look pretty cool! (especially on a silver fastback GT.. with a nuclear reactor in the back, and a flux capacitor inside.. lol.. j/k)<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000010||Wes Janson||07-07-2000||01:08 PM||||Alrighty then. I've heard all I needed to hear. For my first customization project, I will attempt the improbable: hydraulic Gull Wing doors!<P>The coolest thing would be the ability to lower and raise the doors with a pressurization mechanism. Then when the doors are lowered, I'd have latches on the bottom of the frame, and a locking mechanism in the door when it's lowered enough.<P>Challenge is the name of the game, and I think this will be the perfect one for my dad and me to tackle.<P>As for Mr. Fusion, anti-grav generators, and that flux-capacitor... Well, maybe in 15 years.. ;-)<P>Thanks for all of your input, guys!<P>- Janson||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||07-07-2000||04:11 PM||||Good luck with this project, I'd love to hear how you're doing as you work on it.. if you can pull it off, it'll be one of my favorite Fiero mods..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (along with Tom's scoop.. a 3800 SC.. etc.. hehe)<P>be sure to take LOTS of pics.. I don't think anyone's ever tried this before.. I'm really looking forward to see how it turns out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||07-07-2000||04:12 PM||||Almost forgot.. who's better, Rogues or Wraiths?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||12
Z||000013||Taijiguy||07-07-2000||05:39 PM||||OK, so while I was reading all the posts, it occured to me, what if you fashion a hinge mechanism that mounts to the SIDES of the doors, similar in design to a standard hood hinge, only longer. It could be manufactured  so that it collapses tight, and the intial motion is more or less straight out, and then progressively begins to swing upward and away. Saves all the re-fabrication and design of the doors. Properly design the hinges, and you could leave almmost everything as it is, with the exception of hinge covers, and latching system. Hot dang, let's make some gull wing doors!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wes Janson||07-07-2000||08:38 PM||||It's going to take a luttle while to plan this procedure out. My dad has long work hours, so he's counting on me to come up with some viable plans. After that, I'll have to go and scavenge up the parts I need. When I actually get to the project, I don't know. But rest assured, I WILL do this, one way or another. When things start up, I'll make sure to let you all know.<P>And to DaRKLoRD,<P>The Wraiths rock, but the classic Rogues can get the job done twice as fast. ;-)<P>- Janson||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||07-07-2000||08:56 PM||||It would be alot easier and just as trick to do a suicide door.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000016||Wes Janson||07-07-2000||09:01 PM||||We're not going for "easy". We're doing this not only for the coolness of the doors, but also for the challenges it offers. This also gives my dad and me a chance to do some more bonding. As a matter of fact, he okayed the procedure just now. All we need is a plan.<P>And to repeat myself, Gull Wings are just too darn cool!<P>- Janson||||reg||1
Z||000017||Taijiguy||07-08-2000||10:43 AM||||Oh yeah, the other thing about my idea with the "hood hinge" design, is you retain the completely stock appearance. No one knows it's different until they see the door swing up into the air! Jeeze, I may have to look into this now! ||||reg||4
Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||07-08-2000||01:56 PM||||I think the coolness factor of gullwing doors would overshadow any kind of surprise from having stock-looking doors that didn't open like stock doors.<P>that's just my opinion though!! I think both your ideas are good..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think any kind of modification like that makes the car really exotic.. and if I weren't so ****ing tall, I'd consider doing that mod myself.. but I need the sunroof for the extra head room... I suppose I could find a way around that, by putting small windows in the tops of the gullwings.. oh well, I'll worry about that when I can afford it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||Spyder||07-12-2000||12:41 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/zxlambo.jpg"> <P>Ok, How about this!?<BR>Looks like the windows have to be down an inch to work. <BR>But one can install an automatic quick roll down feature like on the Porsche Boxster.<BR>When you pull the door handle the window rolls down an inch as you open the door.<BR>They did add a small triangle frame to the front of the window.  <P>Here is the link to more pics: <A HREF="http://user.tninet.se/~bjx414c/jackesnissane.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://user.tninet.se/~bjx414c/jackesnissane.htm</A> <P>||||reg||3
Z||000020||DaRkLoRD||07-12-2000||06:05 PM||||*DROOLS*<P>OMG..... I WANT THAT CAR!!!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
